Journal
=======

A diary to write in: a page for every day. $.Docs.Journal is the
full guide.

Click SELECT on the Journal's icon on the icon bar to open today's
page and start typing. Click ADJUST for the calendar: the days you
have written on are marked, with their mood and weather. Click a day
to open its page; the arrows turn the months.

On a page:
  Ctrl-T     start a new entry, headed with the time
  Ctrl-D     type the date
  F3         save the page now
  F4         find words anywhere in the journal
  F5         go to a date
  Print      print the page (!Printers must be loaded)
  Ctrl-Shift-Left / Right   the day before / after
  F8 / F9    undo / redo      Ctrl-C, Ctrl-X, Ctrl-V  copy, cut, paste

Choose the day's mood and weather with the buttons at the top of the
page. MENU on a page has Insert > Prompt, for days when it's hard to
know what to write, and Export, to save the page as a text file or a
web page. MENU on the calendar exports a month (or the whole journal)
as text, as a web page or as a Draw file, and prints the month.

Pages are saved as you type (Choices... can turn this off). Each day
is a Text file in $.Journal (year.month.day), so you can read it in
!Edit too; the Journal notices when a page is changed there. Drag a
folder onto the icon to use it as the journal instead.

Password > Lock journal... on the icon bar menu scrambles every page
with a password. Keep it safe: without it the pages can't be read by
anyone, and that includes you.

Check tests the Journal's parts that don't need windows.
